# semilshah.me — server rules
#
# Deploy: this file must sit at the DOMAIN ROOT alongside index.html
#         (Hostinger: public_html/). FTP it like any other file.
#
# Canonical host is the apex, https://semilshah.me — matching `site` in
# site.config.json, the <link rel="canonical"> tags build.js stamps, and
# sitemap.xml. Keep all four in agreement if the canonical ever changes.
#
# NOT handled here, on purpose:
#   - HTTP -> HTTPS. Hostinger already 301s that at the platform level for
#     both hosts. Re-doing it behind their hcdn CDN with a %{HTTPS} test is
#     a known redirect-loop trigger, because the CDN terminates TLS and the
#     origin sees plain HTTP.

RewriteEngine On

# www -> non-www, preserving path and query string.
# NE stops mod_rewrite re-escaping characters that are already encoded.
RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} ^www\.semilshah\.me$ [NC]
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://semilshah.me/$1 [R=301,L,NE]

# --- build tooling is not part of the site --------------------------------
#
# _partials/, build.js, check.js and the config files exist to BUILD the pages;
# nothing on the live site reads them. They were being served as 200s.
#
# _partials/*.html is the one that actually matters: raw fragments carrying
# {{BASE}} placeholders, no <title> and no canonical — thin broken pages if a
# crawler ever finds them.
#
# Blocking here rather than relying on remembering not to upload them, so the
# simple "upload the whole folder" workflow stays safe.

# RedirectMatch throughout, not <FilesMatch>+Require. Tested on this host:
# RedirectMatch works, while "Require all denied" silently did nothing —
# it needs AllowOverride AuthConfig, which this plan does not grant. The
# files kept returning 200 until this was rewritten.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/_partials(/.*)?$
RedirectMatch 404 ^/(build|check)\.js$
RedirectMatch 404 ^/(site\.config|skills)\.json$
RedirectMatch 404 ^/README\.md$
